  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131632/assets/6c33587e4b6ca5ebe9ae3f168e9f9273937a0d74c8de8dea047f6ab9fe2a60ad.png)\n\nThe numbered angle that refers to the same angle as $∠IHG$ is $∠${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "If we trace along the letters of the angle name, from $I$ to $H$ to $G,$ we see that $∠IHG$ refers to the angle $∠2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131632/assets/78021d5a513fcc8d80dee9c60318de3806c0c05ea6c4deb56f1e68076a6343fd.png)\n\nTherefore, $∠2$ is another name for $∠IHG.$",
